0002 — anonymous classes (compiler/decl.rs, classlink.rs).

* Anonymous classes are not final in php-src (only ZEND_ACC_ANON_CLASS is
  set; `final` on one is a parse error), so a class_alias of one can be
  extended (Zend/tests/anon/011) and ReflectionClass::__toString() prints
  "class class@anonymous..." not "final class ..." (gh22681/ReflectionClass_name).
* zend_compile_single_typename does not substitute self/parent inside an
  anonymous class (GH-18373): the type keeps "self"/"parent" like in traits
  (ext/reflection/tests/gh18373).
* Messages that php-src formats with %pS print the whole generated name,
  including the NUL byte and "file:line$n" suffix: "Class %s cannot extend
  ...", "%s %s must implement N abstract method(s)" / "... contains N
  abstract method(s)..." (Zend/tests/anon/gh15994). Method names inside the
  abstract list stay truncated (they are printed with %s).

